      ],
      "message": "p2p: skip parent lookups for orphan announcements that cannot add a candidate\n\nWhen a peer announces the wtxid of a transaction in the orphanage,\nAddTxAnnouncement computes the orphan's missing parents before\nMaybeAddOrphanResolutionCandidate decides whether the peer can become\na resolution candidate. For an orphan with many inputs this means\nthousands of lookups per announcement, and the result is discarded\nwhen the peer is already an announcer or has no room left in its\nannouncement budget.\n\nDo both checks first. The budget check uses the number of inputs as\nan upper bound for the number of missing parents, so a peer close to\nMAX_PEER_TX_ANNOUNCEMENTS may no longer be added as a candidate for\nan orphan whose inputs share parents or whose parents are partly\nknown.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jan Kahmen <jan@turingpoint.de>",
      "committer": {
